redit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          TIFF                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;It's still &lt;em&gt;technically &lt;/em&gt;summer for a few more days, but one indicator that we're already in fall movie season is the Toronto International Film Festival. As is the case every year, the fest showcases features and shorts from across the globe, many of them seemingly destined for awards buzz. I spent a few days at the festival and checked out 25 films, and it's likely you'll have the chance to check many of them out, too. Here are a few of my favorites.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;em&gt;All That She Wants&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143940" class="bucketwrap image large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 8256;         --source-height: 4642;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4642+0+186/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2Ff5%2Fafe3c19947419c916d1921e4505f%2Fatsw-am-d12-250923-705.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4642+0+186/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fa0%2Ff5%2Fafe3c19947419c916d1921e4505f%2Fatsw-am-d12-250923-705.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8256x4642+0+186/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amaz