c%2F260608-mcdolan-nunalleq-09381.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8380x5561+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F9d%2F98%2F853eadd24b1aab5b022fedd3514c%2F260608-mcdolan-nunalleq-09381.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8380x5561+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F9d%2F98%2F853eadd24b1aab5b022fedd3514c%2F260608-mcdolan-nunalleq-09381.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8380x5561+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F9d%2F98%2F853eadd24b1aab5b022fedd3514c%2F260608-mcdolan-nunalleq-09381.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8380x5561+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F9d%2F98%2F853eadd24b1aab5b022fedd3514c%2F260608-mcdolan-nunalleq-09381.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/8380x5561+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F9d%2F98%2F853eadd24b1aab5b022fedd3514c%2F260608-mcdolan-nunalleq-09381.jpg" class="img" alt="Charlotta Hillerdal holds up a wooden doll found in the soil at Nunalleq. " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Charlotta Hillerdal holds up a wooden doll found in the soil at Nunalleq.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          MaryCait Dolan/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Precious objects slowly being excavated&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Archaeologists have been working at this dig site since 2009, according to lead archaeologist Rick Knecht. He says that after thawing permafrost revealed significant numbers of these objects in the early 2000s, the village deliberated and decided to try to save these pieces of their culture.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;They &lt;a href="https://nunalleq.org/" target="_blank"&gt;include&lt;/a&gt; hand-carved animals, grass rope, sewing needles, ornate wooden masks and pieces of kayaks.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;According to the archaeologists, the frozen ground has helped preserve artifacts composed of organic material, which they say would have likely eroded under different conditions.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5966568-102" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5966568-102" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;The team, Knecht says, is mostly made up of volunteers and has a shoestring budget with funding from the Pacific Northwest Archaeological Society and the Daughters of the American Revolution, among others.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;The whole archaeological site is about the size of two Olympic-size pools, but the emergency dig area is smaller, about the size of a backyard pool. It's a hole that has been dug around the buried remnants of several sod houses that date back 400 to 500 years.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143709" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1600;         --source-height: 539;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F45%2Ff3%2F5ff3b4024fe89ae499aff5f7a27b%2Fartifacts-1.jpg" class="img" alt="Kenneth McElroy examines pieces of leather he excavated from the Nunalleq dig on June 8, 2026." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Kenneth McElroy examines pieces of leather he excavated from the Nunalleq dig on June 8.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          MaryCait Dolan/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digging against time&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Charlotta Hillerdal, who has been part of this excavation for over 15 years, was home in Scotland when she heard about the storm damage.&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;aside id="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" class="mid-story-recommendations-mount-piano" aria-label="recommended stories"&gt;&lt;/aside&gt;    &lt;!-- END ID="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" CLASS="MID-STORY-RECOMMENDATIONS-MOUNT-PIANO" ARIA-LABEL="RECOMMENDED STORIES" --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"I was crying," Hillerdal said. "It was a horrible feeling."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;Knecht said that since the dig began, they've watched the Bering Sea creep closer and closer to the site. Shorelines in this part of Alaska are&lt;a href="https://www.climatehubs.usda.gov/hubs/northwest/topic/storm-brewing-climate-change-and-coastal-storms-western-alaska" target="_blank"&gt; now more vulnerable&lt;/a&gt; to erosion due, in part, to decreasing sea ice and permafrost thaw. Both are fueled by human-caused climate change.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5966568-103" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5966568-103" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Last October's storm closed the distance even more. Now, at some high tides, seawater can reach into the pit.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"It's every bit as tough as working in front of bulldozers," Knecht explained.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;In October, the flooding was so extensive that the site was covered by feet of water. When it receded, it took many valuable objects with it. They're worried that could happen again.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5966568-104" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5966568-104" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Knecht said they hope to return to the site next summer, though they're still raising the money to do so through a GoFundMe campaign and Quinhagak Heritage Inc., the nonprofit that oversees the dig.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"I'll be damned if I'm going to leave this for the waves," Knecht said. "It's like you might as well take those pieces of artwork we're finding and skip it off into the Bering Sea."&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143713" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 9504;         --source-height: 6336;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/9504x6336+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F3e%2Ffb%2Fcb1cea0d415285df38c500859b6d%2F260609-mcdolan-nunalleqmuseum-01039.jpg" class="img" alt="Stephanie Harold creates watercolor illustrations of artifacts excavated from the Nunalleq dig site. " loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Stephanie Harold creates watercolor illustrations of artifacts excavated from the Nunalleq dig site.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          MaryCait Dolan/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;h3 class="edTag"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;"When you know that you come from a people that were so resilient … you get a boost" &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;   &lt;p&gt;At the Nunalleq Culture and Archaeology Center — a museum-style building and lab — these pieces of Quinhagak's past&lt;a href="https://alaskapublic.org/news/2023-09-05/quinhagaks-museum-has-the-worlds-largest-collection-of-yupik-artifacts-and-archeologists-keep-finding-more" target="_blank"&gt; are available&lt;/a&gt; for their direct descendants to access, along with the public.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"We all as humans want to know who we are and where we come from, and having the Nunalleq there for us strengthens that," said Elizabeth Church, director of Quinhagak Heritage Inc., which manages the center as well as the dig.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resnx-s1-5966568-105" class="bucketwrap internallink insettwocolumn inset2col"&gt;                     &lt;!-- END CLASS="BUCKET IMG" --&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;     &lt;!-- END ID="RESNX-S1-5966568-105" CLASS="BUCKETWRAP INTERNALLINK INSETTWOCOLUMN INSET2COL " --&gt;    &lt;p&gt;Church said seeing the artifacts exploded onto the beach was traumatic. It underscored the community's desire to steward their ancestors' belongings.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;div id="resg-s1-143711" class="bucketwrap image x-large"&gt;             &lt;div     class="imagewrap has-source-dimensions"     data-crop-type=""     style="         --source-width: 1600;         --source-height: 539;     " &gt;         &lt;picture&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/webp/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/webp" /&gt;             &lt;source srcset="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 400w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/900/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 900w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1200/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 1200w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1600/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 1600w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1800/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 1800w, https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/2400/quality/85/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg 2400w" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg" sizes="(min-width: 1350px) 953px, (min-width: 1025px) calc(100vw - 395px), (min-width: 768px) calc(100vw - 60px), calc(100vw - 30px)" class="img" type="image/jpeg" /&gt;             &lt;img src="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/1100/quality/50/format/jpeg/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg" data-template="https://npr.brightspotcdn.com/dims3/default/strip/false/crop/1600x539+0+0/resize/{width}/quality/{quality}/format/{format}/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fnpr-brightspot.s3.amazonaws.com%2F72%2F83%2F1654ef0c4ef09091d86804cde656%2Fartifacts-3.jpg" class="img" alt="Kenneth McElroy excavates an artifact from the Nunalleq dig site. Monica Shah places wooden artifacts in a polyethylene glycol solution." loading="lazy" /&gt;         &lt;/picture&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div class="credit-caption"&gt;     &lt;div class="caption-wrap"&gt;         &lt;div class="caption" aria-label="Image caption"&gt;             &lt;p&gt;                 Kenneth McElroy excavates an artifact from the Nunalleq dig site. Monica Shah places wooden artifacts in a polyethylene glycol solution.                 &lt;b class="credit" aria-label="Image credit"&gt;                                          MaryCait Dolan/KYUK                                      &lt;/b&gt;                 &lt;b class="hide-caption"&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/p&gt;         &lt;/div&gt;               &lt;b class="toggle-caption"&gt;               &lt;svg class="icon icon--info"&gt;&lt;use href="#icon-info"&gt;&lt;/use&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;               &lt;b&gt;&lt;/b&gt;             &lt;/b&gt;     &lt;/div&gt;       &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;/div&gt;    &lt;p&gt;"They are interwoven into us as people, and we feel a great sense of responsibility to care for them well, and to take them into the future with us," Church said.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;There's evidence of people adapting to environmental change and making technological progress.&lt;/p&gt;   &lt;p&gt;"When you know that you come from a people that were so resilient and so capable and so talented and so smart — you get a boost," Church said. "It's amazing."&lt;/p&gt;       &lt;p&gt;She said that with fall storm season fast approaching, the scramble is urgent to recover what they can of this past.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description>
